# SHELL SCRIPTS MUST CHECK OUT WITH LF, AND THIS IS NOT A STYLE PREFERENCE.
#
# Found 2026-08-23 the first time a mutation sweep was run in a git worktree, as
# docs/OWNER_DOCKET.md requires them to be. A fresh checkout gave
# tools/sweep_*.sh CRLF endings, and the effect was SILENT rather than loud:
#
#   * the preflight parses the mutant table with `^"(.*?)"$` in MULTILINE mode,
#     and with CRLF the character before each newline is , not the closing
#     quote. It matched nothing and reported "linted 0 mutants, 0 do not build"
#     -- a clean pass over an empty set;
#   * bash reading `#!/usr/bin/env bash` and CRLF-terminated array entries
#     carries the  into every anchor, so no anchor can ever match its file.
#
# EVERY sweep in tools/ was affected, not just the new one. They had only ever
# been run in the tree they were authored in, where the working copy was already
# LF, so nothing had exercised a checkout of them.
#
# ENFORCED-BY: this rule, plus the preflight's own refusal to run on an empty
# mutant table -- a guard that lints nothing must fail, not pass.
*.sh text eol=lf
tools/*.py text eol=lf

# Committed binary evidence: never touch.
*.bin -text
*.zcap -text
*.zcorpus -text
tests/abi/golden/** -text
captures/** -text

